{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\n`/health` on the MCP server returns 200 without ever touching the ticket store, so a container\nwith **no store at all** passes both the container HEALTHCHECK and the blue-green readiness\ngate. A structurally broken deploy is indistinguishable from a healthy one.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_health.py:118-120` — the handler returns `JSONResponse({\"in_flight\": gauge.value})`\n  and nothing else.\n- `infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp:56-57` — the container HEALTHCHECK is a plain 200 check on\n  `/health`.\n- `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:130` — the blue-green readiness gate promotes on that same probe.\n- `src/rebar/mcp_server.py:759-761` — the boot sweep is guarded by `if os.path.isdir(_tracker)`\n  and emits NOTHING when the store is absent; the comment at `:752` states the intent\n  (\"a missing store / import / sweep error never aborts boot\"), so not even the `debug` line at\n  `:769` fires (that needs an exception).\n\nCorroborating log evidence: 60 SSM invocations spanning 2026-08-06 to 2026-08-25 contain zero\nmatches for `tickets-tracker`, `not initialized`, or `ticket init` — exactly what the code\npredicts. (Container logs use `driver: journald` at `docker-compose.yml:72,258,306,383` and no\nCloudWatch log group exists for them, so there is no remote log trail either.)\n\n## Why this matters\n\nThis is the reason the missing-store defect went unnoticed since deployment. Log-and-continue on\nboot is a defensible posture on its own; combining it with a health probe that cannot observe the\nstore means nothing in the pipeline can ever report the failure.\n\n## How `expected` is computed (the field the whole refusal turns on)\n\n`expected` is TRUE iff the deployment has EXPLICITLY declared where its store lives — concretely\n`config.tracker_dir_override()`, i.e. the `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` env override is set and non-empty.\nIt is FALSE when nothing is configured and the path is merely the default relative\n`.tickets-tracker` resolved against the repo root.\n\nDeliberately read from the ENV OVERRIDE ALONE, not the parsed config, for two reasons: a health\nprobe must not be able to fail (or hang) on config parsing, and the repo's\n`check_config_ownership` gate reserves `load_config` to approved seams. A project that instead\ndeclares a non-default `tracker.dir` in config therefore reports `expected: false` and simply\ndoes not get the strict gate — it degrades to the pre-change behaviour rather than misreporting.\nThe deployment surface that matters here (the mcp compose service) sets the env var explicitly.\n\nThis is what makes the safety story concrete — and the STATE OF THE BOX MATTERS, so state it\nas of now rather than as a standing property. When this was first written the mcp service set\nno tracker dir, so `expected` was false and the gate was inert. That is NO LONGER TRUE: the\nsibling change kilted-nuclear-bronco now sets `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR=/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets`,\nverified on the live container. The store is meanwhile absent (a partial clone with no\nresolvable HEAD), so the box currently sits at `expected=true, present=false` — exactly the\nrefusal condition.\n\nThe gate is therefore LIVE, not inert, and landing this before the store works would refuse\npromotion of every mcp container with `mcp-store-missing`, blocking mcp deploys entirely. That\nis the gate behaving as designed; the ordering is the thing that must be controlled. This\nticket accordingly `depends_on` fathomable-yester-thrip (the poisoned-volume fix) and must not\nland until a real clone is in place.\n\n## What `present` means, and why it is not HEAD-strict\n\n`present` is exactly `os.path.isdir(path)` — the directory exists. It is deliberately NOT \"a\nusable store\" (a resolvable HEAD), and that choice is load-bearing:\n\nProvisioning is BACKGROUNDED (`provision_store &` then `exec \"$@\"`) because the ~200k-commit\nclone outruns the 120s blue-green readiness deadline. A freshly started container therefore has\na legitimately empty, HEAD-less tracker dir for MINUTES while its clone runs. A HEAD-strict\n`present` would report that healthy container as not-ready, the gate would roll it back, and\nthe next tick would start another — reproducing the rollback loop `unfit-beneficial-whimbrel`\ndocuments. The probe answers \"is a store dir here at all\", not \"is it converged\".\n\n**Residual limitation, stated rather than implied:** a POISONED store — files but no usable\n`.git`, the state observed in production — satisfies `isdir` and reports `present: True`. This\nprobe does not detect that and is not the mechanism that should: `fathomable-yester-thrip`\n(change 2244, merged) re-clones a store whose HEAD does not resolve. This gate catches the\nABSENT-store deploy; the entrypoint catches the poisoned-store deploy. Neither subsumes the\nother, and the acceptance criteria below are scoped to the absent case only.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\nAll proven by `tests/unit/test_mcp_health_store_status.py` (8 tests), each mutation-checked.\n\n- [x] `/health` reports the store as a structured object — `{path, present, expected}`.\n      Proof: `test_present_store_is_reported_present`,\n      `test_absent_store_is_reported_absent_and_expected_when_a_dir_is_configured`\n- [x] The gate FAILS OPEN on an unreadable or malformed signal, matching autodeploy's posture.\n      Proof: `test_probe_never_raises_even_when_resolution_fails`\n- [x] The refusal is keyed on `expected AND NOT present`, never on absence alone, so a\n      deployment that never configured a tracker dir is not marked unhealthy.\n      Proof: `test_no_configured_dir_is_not_expected`\n- [x] The refusal is observable under its own name (`mcp-store-missing`).\n      Proof: `test_autodeploy_gate_names_the_storeless_refusal`\n- [x] Boot emits one log line naming the tracker path when the store is absent, and is quiet\n      when it exists. Proof: `test_boot_sweep_warns_naming_the_path_when_the_store_is_absent`,\n      `test_boot_sweep_is_quiet_and_does_not_raise_when_the_store_exists`\n- [x] `store_status()` never raises for an ordinary resolution fault, with ONE deliberate\n      exception: a removed-but-still-set load-bearing input fails hard rather than being\n      reported as merely degraded.\n      Proof: `test_probe_never_raises_even_when_resolution_fails`,\n      `test_a_removed_load_bearing_input_fails_hard_instead_of_being_reported` — mutating the\n      handler to swallow it yields DID NOT RAISE.\n\n\n## Verification\n\n    .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_mcp_health_store_status.py -q -p no:randomly\n    .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py -q -p no:randomly\n\nPer-criterion proving tests:\n\n| criterion | proving test |\n|---|---|\n| gate consumes the field and refuses | `test_storeless_container_is_not_promoted_when_a_store_is_expected` |\n| fails open on a body with no store field | `test_health_without_a_store_field_still_promotes` |\n| keyed on expected, not absence | `test_storeless_container_IS_promoted_when_no_store_is_expected` |\n| named refusal reason | `test_autodeploy_gate_names_the_storeless_refusal` |\n| boot names the absent path | `test_boot_sweep_warns_naming_the_path_when_the_store_is_absent` |\n| probe never raises / present-store branch runs | `test_probe_never_raises_even_when_resolution_fails`, `test_boot_sweep_is_quiet_and_does_not_raise_when_the_store_exists` |\n\nTeeth: gating on `present` alone (dropping `expected`) turns the two promote-cases RED; removing\nthe gate turns the refusal case RED; an early return in the sweep turns the liveness anchor RED."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787816727617611001,"uuid":"9ccccf5a-7298-4b77-9e0a-4469128efca2"}